      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An acute dose of morphine increased brain tryptophan in mice. This effect was not prevented by naloxone nor was it produced by other narcotic analgesics. Dextrorphan, but not levorphanol, had a similar effect to morphine. A large dose of tryptophan had no effect on the antinociceptive action of morphine in mice. Morphine increased brain tryptophan in rats. This effect was prevented by naloxone. A large dose of tryptophan antagonised the antinociceptive action of morphine in the rat."},
